}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(5,2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533974 true] [17592186275488 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275489 13194139533974 true] [17592186275488 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533974 true] [17592186275488 1041 "field-1" 13194139533974 true] [17592186275488 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275489 13194139533974 true] [17592186275488 1110 #uuid "ba6f87da-c319-57a2-ad8a-fe94131112fe" 13194139533974 true] [17592186275489 1034 "\\frac{(x-5)^2}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^2}{25}" 13194139533974 true] [17592186275489 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533974 true] [17592186275489 1111 #uuid "0c833d29-7783-5eba-b328-e441a01cc990" 13194139533974 true] [17592186275490 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275491 13194139533974 true] [17592186275490 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275493 13194139533974 true] [17592186275490 1089 "q-278315" 13194139533974 true] [17592186275490 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533974 true] [17592186275490 1100 "The center of the ellipse $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9}=1$ is located at the point$\\,($\n{{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$).$" 13194139533974 true] [17592186275490 1113 #uuid "8394b6cf-2348-5071-945d-1dada4ceddaf" 13194139533974 true] [17592186275490 1145 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=3$ and $k=2,$ so the center is located at $(3,2).$" 13194139533974 true] [17592186275491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275492 13194139533974 true] [17592186275491 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 131941